.TH HOTSPOTD 8 "2026-09-09" "hotspotd 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
hotspotd \- WiFi access point manager that tells you why it cannot start
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hotspotd
.RI [ options ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hotspotd
brings up a WiFi access point on a Linux machine, sharing the connection the
machine already has.  The access point runs on its own virtual interface, so
the uplink you are sharing is not taken away from you.
.PP
What sets it apart from the alternatives is
.BR "hotspotd doctor" :
before anything is touched, it works out whether an access point can run here
at all \- whether the radio supports AP mode, which channels the regulatory
domain actually permits beaconing on, whether an AP may coexist with the
client connection and under what constraint, and whether the mandatory access
control policy will let hostapd read its own configuration.  Every one of
those produces, in other tools, a failure message that points somewhere else.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Report whether an access point can start on this machine, and if not, which
constraint is in the way and what to do about it.  Exits 0 when ready, 2 when
blocked.  Run it as root for a complete picture: an unprivileged
.BR iw (8)
cannot read the radio's capabilities.
.TP
.BI up " SSID"
Start the access point.  With no
.I SSID
the settings saved by a previous
.B \-\-save
are used.  The passphrase is asked for interactively unless
.BR \-\-password ,
.B \-\-open
or
.B $HOTSPOTD_PASS
supplies one.
.TP
.B down
Stop the running access point and undo every change that starting it made.
.TP
.B status
Show the running access point, how long it has been up, and the clients
connected to it with their addresses and host names.
.TP
.B enable
Start the saved access point at boot, through
.BR hotspotd.service (8).
.TP
.B disable
Stop starting it at boot.
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be given before or after the command.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fIIFACE\fR
WiFi interface to use.  The first wireless interface found is the default.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASS\fR
WPA2 passphrase, 8 to 63 characters.  Passing it here makes it visible to
every user on the machine through
.BR ps (1);
prefer the interactive prompt or
.BR $HOTSPOTD_PASS .
.TP
.B \-\-open
Run an unencrypted network.  Anyone in range can join it and read the traffic
of everyone on it.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-channel " " \fIN\fR
Channel to use.  The default is the channel the uplink is already on, because
many radios \- Intel's AX2xx series among them \- permit a client and an
access point simultaneously only while both stay on one channel.
.TP
.B \-\-ap\-interface \fIIFACE\fR
Name for the virtual AP interface.  Default
.BR ap0 .
An interface that already exists is never taken over.
.TP
.B \-\-subnet \fIA.B.C\fR
First three octets of the hotspot network.  Default
.BR 192.168.12 .
.TP
.B \-\-uplink \fIIFACE\fR
Interface to share the internet from.  Defaults to the WiFi uplink.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-nat
Do not share any internet connection.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dhcp
Do not run dnsmasq; clients must configure addresses themselves.
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Do not broadcast the SSID.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Write these settings to the profile so
.B hotspotd up
and the boot service can reuse them.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output, for
.B doctor
and
.BR status .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable coloured output.  The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable does the same.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hotspotd/hotspotd.conf
Saved settings, including the passphrase.  Mode 0600.
.TP
.I /run/hotspotd/state.json
The running access point and every change made to bring it up, so that
.B down
reverses exactly those and nothing else.
.TP
.I /etc/hostapd.hotspotd.conf
Generated hostapd configuration.  The location is chosen to satisfy the
active AppArmor policy and is removed when the hotspot stops.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed; the reason is printed on standard error.
.TP
.B 2
.B doctor
found a blocking problem.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOTSPOTD_PASS
WPA2 passphrase, used when
.B \-\-password
is not given.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable coloured output when set to any value.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the machine before trying anything:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo hotspotd doctor
.RE
.PP
Start an access point, typing the passphrase at the prompt:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo hotspotd up Home
.RE
.PP
Start one and remember it, then have it come back after a reboot:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo hotspotd up Home \-\-save
.br
.B sudo hotspotd enable
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hostapd (8),
.BR dnsmasq (8),
.BR iw (8),
.BR firewall-cmd (1),
.BR nft (8)
.SH BUGS
Report them at
.UR https://github.com/emirberasoguk/hotspotd/issues
.UE .
Output of
.B hotspotd doctor \-\-json
from a radio hotspotd gets wrong is especially useful: it becomes a test case.
